  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added IHealthService.GetEarliestAccessibleDateTime(CancellationToken) — reports the earliest UTC DateTime from which the device currently allows health-data reads, so consumers can size sync windows without per-platform branching. On Android: returns DateTime.MinValue when READ_HEALTH_DATA_HISTORY is granted; otherwise returns (firstPermissionGrantAt - 30 days) matching Health Connect's \"30 days prior to when any permission was first granted\" rule. The first-grant timestamp is persisted to MAUI Preferences on the none-to-some transition inside RequestPermissions (the platform exposes no API to retrieve it). Falls back to (now - 30 days) when no anchor is persisted (e.g. after Clear Storage, or existing installs upgrading from earlier library versions). On iOS: returns DateTime.MinValue (HealthKit has no documented cap).",
